# K-Net: Ten Generations

## A Roadmap from the Acropolis to Yggdrasil

---

# Abstract

K-Net is not a static architecture—it is a digital civilization in evolution. While Paper 01 introduced the current MVP (Generation 1: The Acropolis), this paper presents the complete ten-generation roadmap that defines K-Net's long-term trajectory. The ten generations are: (1) Acropolis Architecture, (2) Specialized Pyramid, (3) Overlapping Circles, (4) Integrated Knowledge City, (5) Parliament of Minds, (6) Inverted Pyramid of Unity, (7) Knowledge Hourglass, (8) Wisdom Diamond, (9) Pyramid of Commonality, and (10) Yggdrasil. Each generation represents a distinct stage in the maturation of K-Net's four core components—Knowledge Sphere, Shield, Why Engine, and Wisdom Mode. This paper defines the vision, the incremental philosophy behind the roadmap, and the dependency graph linking all ten generations. No new implementation or benchmarks are reported; this is purely a vision and roadmap document.

---

# Keywords

K-Net, roadmap, ten generations, vision, Yggdrasil, knowledge evolution, ternary logic, Wisdom Mode

